aic8800: lower the default debug log level to errors only

Both AIC8800 modules ship a debug mask that enables every level. The BSP's
aicwf_dbg_level_bsp logs each step of chip power-on and firmware download; the
FullMAC driver's aicwf_dbg_level additionally enables LOGFW, which relays the
firmware's own log. Together they emit enough to fill a console faster than a
login can be typed. Lower both to LOGERROR.

The level must be compiled in rather than set from modprobe.d. The BSP's is not a
module_param at all, and while the FullMAC driver's is, a module_param is only
applied by a configuration file that reaches the image -- so a device that does
not carry etc/modprobe.d/aic8800.conf would boot verbose. Compiling the default
makes quietness a property of the module itself, and leaves the module_param as
the knob for raising the level again (aicwf_dbg_level=0x40f re-enables the
firmware log).

These are the two SDIO hunks of radxa's fix-Lower-the-debugging-log-level.patch
(Feng Zhang <feng@radxa.com>), carried here because the full patch also touches
the PCIE and USB trees this board does not build, and `git apply` is
all-or-nothing.

diff --git a/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_bsp/aic_bsp_main.c b/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_bsp/aic_bsp_main.c
--- a/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_bsp/aic_bsp_main.c
+++ b/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_bsp/aic_bsp_main.c
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@
 #define DRV_AUTHOR            "AICSemi"
 #define DRV_VERS_MOD          "1.0"

-int aicwf_dbg_level_bsp = LOGERROR|LOGINFO|LOGDEBUG|LOGTRACE;
+int aicwf_dbg_level_bsp = LOGERROR;

 struct semaphore aicbsp_probe_semaphore;

diff --git a/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c b/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
--- a/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
+++ b/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
@@ -535,7 +535,7 @@ static const int rwnx_hwq2uapsd[NL80211_NUM_ACS] = {


 extern uint8_t scanning;
-int aicwf_dbg_level = LOGERROR|LOGINFO|LOGDEBUG|LOGTRACE|LOGFW;
+int aicwf_dbg_level = LOGERROR;
 module_param(aicwf_dbg_level, int, 0660);
 #ifdef CONFIG_DYNAMIC_PWR
 int dynamic_pwr = 1;
